1.3: # of polling stations visited on election day</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="N/A"></target>
     <actual value="1.1. 157

1.2: 100%

1.3: 79 polling stations were visited on Special Voting Day and 1,108 polling stations
were visited on election day"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1 An UN strategic messaging campaign is launched to educate, inform, and update Iraqi voters on election preparations, and UN activities in support of elections in advance of and on election day</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="272116" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1. # of communication activities conducted in the framework of the UN strategic messaging campaign; 

2.2. # of briefings of UN partners, MS, and other international partners held.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="N/A"></target>
     <actual value="2.1. Tools used during the campaign included: approximately 900 social media posts (in Arabic,
Kurdish and English, across Facebook, Instagram, Twitter and YouTube); 40 murals in 11
governorates; 20 web stories; 14 videos; nine fact sheets; seven media interviews by the Special
Representative and her deputy; two press conferences; one digital dialogue moderated by the
Special Representative; one online workshop for youth; promotional materials, such as
#Vote4Iraq t-shirts, stickers and buttons; and engagement with Iraqi artists and influencers.
Collectively, all social media posts earned more than 3.8 million impressions on UNAMI&#x2019;s social
media channels alone.

2.2 N/A"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
